          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em evolutionary derivative
            or “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+derivative"} Fréchet derivative
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
            of differential functions” (
            %a{:href => "#Olver93"}> Olver 93, def. 5.24
            )) is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            depending on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jets"} jets
            of a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"}> field bundle
            ”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FieldDependentSections"}
            below) along the prolongation of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evolutionary+vector+field"} evolutionary vector field
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+operator"} differential operator
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+tangent+bundle"} vertical tangent bundle
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and as such is usefully related to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+derivative"} Euler-Lagrange derivative
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOperatorDerivativeOfLagrangianFunction"}
            and prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeDerivativeIsDerivationViaAdjointFrechetDerivatives"}
            below).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In the following
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
            are considered in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            and in particular
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            means
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+vector+bundle"} smooth vector bundle
          #FieldDependentSections.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"}> field
                \-dependent
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            %p For
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi fb
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \overset{fb}{\longrightarrow} \Sigma
            %p
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi fb
                        %mo ′
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E' \overset{fb'}{\longrightarrow} \Sigma
            %p
              any other
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
              over the same base space (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"}> spacetime
              ), we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi J
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi J
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi jb
                      %mo *
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi J
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi DiffOp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{J^\infty_\Sigma(E)}(E')
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\Gamma_{J^\infty_\Sigma(E)}( jb^\ast E' )
                    \\;=\;
                    Hom_\Sigma(J^\infty_\Sigma(E), E')
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    DiffOp(E,E')
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+sections"} space of sections
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+bundles"} pullback of bundles
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
